From 50e9a0baa704800a3291e5d493649e551b316b03 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AERA | Erez Yaary <yaary@me.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 14:20:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] conn.c: the log kept open, closed a second after a line at
 most (Erez's middle way)

Erez, 17 Nov 2026: "build the log middle way", and every AERA app that
opens and closes its log that often to change with it. Each line was
an open, a write and a close: about 143 ms a line on his DFB1's IDE
(common/tests/slowdisk: the close after a 1 KB write 140 ms, the write
1.4 ms), 346 ms on a stock Falcon, and a TLS connect's 30 lines ate
laut.fm's 5 s wait for the request (EPlay, his log of 17 Nov).

Now the file stays open and each line is a write to it at once. It is
closed (GEMDOS writes the FAT and the directory, the disk then holds
it whole) in the event wait once a line has waited a second
(conn_log_idle, called from gem.c's event calls, weak: only where
conn.c is linked), never inside a TLS handshake; at once before a
connection (open_plain), at an error's line (" !! "), at a crash's
report (conn_log_append), at conn_log_flush (an app's save, the quit),
when the log is switched off or named anew, and at appl_exit. A freeze
loses at most the last second's lines, none from before a connection.
start_tls no longer closes right after the handshake, inside the
server's wait for the request.

tests/loghold: the counts are writes and closes now (a line one write;
one open for a job), and the middle way's own: closed a second on, not
again with nothing new, an error closed at once, a flush closed, another
name the first file closed. 39 checks, all passed; connslice, connhosts,
langs and translate pass; conn.c and gem.c cross-compile (-Werror).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SZeNoDozTmbWt4s2sFN9eL
